BetterMyAdmin follows phpMyAdmin's main branch. The commit it currently
matches is recorded in docs/reference/reference-commit.txt, and every
upstream commit since the first one is listed, with what we did about it,
in tools/upstream/ledger.json.

What comes from phpMyAdmin:

- The behaviour, pages, controls, interface text, settings and their
  defaults, generated SQL and export formats, as specified in docs/features
  from phpMyAdmin's source code.
- The translations in packages/i18n/po, made by phpMyAdmin's translators
  and imported from phpMyAdmin's catalogues.
- The look of the pmahomme, original, bootstrap, metro and other
  phpMyAdmin themes (apps/web/public/themes, packages/ui/src/themes).
- The documentation in docs-site, adapted from phpMyAdmin's documentation.
  The full list of phpMyAdmin's contributors is in docs-site/credits.rst.
- Test cases and expected outputs taken from phpMyAdmin's own test suite
  (fixtures under packages/*/test/fixtures and tests/parity).
- Fixes and changes made in phpMyAdmin after BetterMyAdmin was first
  specified, ported one commit at a time. Each one is recorded in
  tools/upstream/ledger.json with its author, and the CHANGELOG entry of a
  sync names the phpMyAdmin commits it ports and who wrote them.

